# Threat Model

HDEX Q1 is designed to defend against the following threat classes.

| Threat                         | Protection                                 |
| ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------ |
| Unauthorized filesystem access | Explicit mount restrictions                |
| Directory traversal            | Canonical path validation                  |
| Symlink and hardlink escape    | Filesystem verification                    |
| Sandbox escape                 | Process and filesystem isolation           |
| Malicious workers              | Worker verification and policy enforcement |
| Policy tampering               | Signature verification                     |
| Job tampering                  | Job hashing and signature validation       |
| Dependency poisoning           | Lockfile and integrity verification        |
| Command injection              | No-shell execution                         |
| Secret leakage                 | Environment scrubbing and log redaction    |
| Unauthorized local API access  | Authentication and authorization           |
| Resource exhaustion            | CPU, memory, process, and disk limits      |
| Audit tampering                | Tamper-evident audit chain                 |
| Offline bypass                 | Offline verification tests                 |

